// x-builtin-effects-09: under a restored registration image the check skips
// the defaults a call through a package interface val omits.
//
// The image writes a function type's own lambda id only, so `val rand`'s type
// comes back with no lambda ids; CallSite::check_omitted_defaults finds no
// definition and leaves rand's `#start: 'a = 0.0` / `#end: 'a = 1.0` to the
// bind, after the check has decided the cells. A cold compile checks them.
//
// commands (fresh cache; the first --check compiles cold and writes the
// registration entry, every later command restores it):
//   export XDG_CACHE_HOME=$(mktemp -d)
//   graphix --check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-builtin-effects-09.gx
//   graphix design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-builtin-effects-09.gx
//   graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-builtin-effects-09.gx
//   graphix-fuzz check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-builtin-effects-09.gx
//
// expected: the program is well typed (x: f64); every run prints a number.
// observed: --check exit 0; the run with the registration restored is refused,
//   "in: rand::rand(#clock: null) | in: 0.0 | type mismatch 'a: _ does not
//   contain f64", exit 1; --no-cache prints a number, exit 0; graphix-fuzz
//   check: "DIVERGENCE — the check accepted what the build refused", exit 1.
//
// The same skip makes a warm --check accept an ill-typed call. With the
// registration entry present, `graphix --check` on the one-line program
//   rand::rand(#clock: null) + 1
// exits 0, while `graphix --no-cache --check` refuses it ("cannot compute
// ..: f64 + i64"), as design/parallel_compile.md says the check must.
let x = never();
x <- rand::rand(#clock: null);
println(x);
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0))
